  "description": "TINFEC crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C46 H52 Br4 Cl2 Eu4 N4 O18 2+,2(Cl1 1-),6(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1B (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu2B (Eu) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.593-4.088 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.44-115.46°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu4L2Cl2(OH)4(H2O)4(MeOH)2]·2Cl·7MeOH·2H2O (H2L = bis(5-bromo-3-methoxysalicylidene)ethylene-1,2-phenylenediamine). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
